Read-Only Properties
If you want an attribute to be read-only, define only the @property  decorator (the
getter) and omit the @name.setter  method. Attempting to set the attribute will
then raise an AttributeError . class Person:
def __init__(self, name):
        self._name = name
@property
def name(self):
# Getter
return self._name
@name.setter
def name(self, new_name):
# Setter
        self._name = new_name 
@name.deleter
def name(self):
del self._name
p = Person("Alice")
print(p.name)
# Alice
del p.name
print(p.name)
# AttributeError: 'Person' object has no attrib
